**Operating income is not applicable for JPMorgan Chase.** As a bank holding company, JPMorgan does not report an "operating income" line in its income statement. Its statement runs from net revenue to provision for credit losses, then noninterest expense, then income before income tax expense, then net income.

The closest comparable measure would be income before income tax expense. For fiscal 2025 I estimate that at roughly $73–75 billion, on net income of about $57 billion. That figure is from memory, not checked against the filing, and it is not operating income.

